    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0753" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Peru/729: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-01T11:00:00-05:00">May 1, 1943—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>623. Supplementing my telegram no. 601, April 28, 5 p.m.<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d610-f1"/> The Finance Minister has just informed me that President
                    Prado does not consider the proposal acceptable in view of a conversation in
                    which Duggan<anchor n="53" xml:id="d610-f2"/> is said to have promised to urge
                    reconsideration of the article 3 matter. Since I have no other information in
                    the above regard the Department’s comments would be appreciated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d610-f1" n="52" xml:id="d610-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d610-f2" n="53" xml:id="d610-f2-content">
                <p>Laurence Duggan, Adviser on Political Relations. For correspondence on the trip
                    of Vice President Wallace and Mr. Duggan to certain American Republics including
                    Peru, see <ref target="frus1943v05#pg_55">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >v</hi>, pp. 55</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
